    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i keep getting this SettingWithCopyWarning in my notebook. i'm trying to do something like df[df['col'] > 5]['new_col'] = val but it keeps throwing the warning. can u explain why this happens and how i should actually do it? thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The `SettingWithCopyWarning` occurs because pandas isn't sure if you are modifying a view or a copy of your original DataFrame. This ambiguity can lead to unpredictable changes. To avoid this, you should use the `.loc` indexer for assignment. You can rewrite your code as `df.loc[df['col'] > 5, 'new_col'] = val`, which explicitly tells pandas to make the assignment to the original DataFrame.",
      "source": "target",
